Z||000009||Sage||11-23-2001||10:21 AM||||Dave;<P>Trade with Roger!  Wheather you drive it, store it, show it or sell it, you won't regret it.<BR>JMO<P>Had a buddy with a 66 Vette conv. that needed completely restored.  A friend of his offered to trade a TVR Griffith (English fiberglass body racing car, somewhat rare) for the Vette.  He asked me what I would do, I told him keep the Vette no contest.  The man even trailered the Griffith to his house and let him look it over for a few weeks.  While it was sitting in his drive way, 3 people came and offered to buy it.  One offered $20,000 and the Grif needed allot of work too.  I know what Roger has is not a 66, but a Vette is a Vette is a Vette!  Unless you have one allready, it would be a great addition to your stable.<P>Like I said, just my opinion, and I know you didn't ask for it, was just compelled to share it with you in case you needed some "nudging"!  LOL<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
